3.  **Mechanical Shearing:** This typically causes microangiopathic hemolytic anemia (MAHA) with schistocytes on the blood smear and often thrombocytopenia (e.g., TTP, HUS, DIC). While thrombocytopenia is present, leukopenia and the other systemic features (rash, joint pain, pleuritis, proteinuria) are not typical of primary mechanical shearing disorders.
