    *   The standard site for thoracentesis is typically in the midaxillary line, one intercostal space below the upper level of the effusion, to avoid the lung and major vessels/nerves.
    *   The needle is inserted *above* the rib to avoid the neurovascular bundle running along the *inferior* border of the rib.

