3.  **Determine the effect of α1 receptor activation:** Activation (agonism) of α1 receptors causes smooth muscle contraction.
4.  **Apply this to the eye muscles:**
    *   Activation of α1 receptors on the pupillary dilator muscle will cause its contraction. Contraction of the dilator muscle leads to pupillary dilation (mydriasis).
    *   Activation of α1 receptors on the ciliary muscle will cause its contraction. Contraction of the ciliary muscle leads to accommodation (focusing for near vision) and potentially increased aqueous humor outflow (though this is more complex and involves other pathways).
5.  **Evaluate the options:**
