    *   C: Relaxation of the pupillary sphincter muscle (incorrect, α1 agonists don't directly target the sphincter, which is primarily controlled by parasympathetic nerves via M3 receptors; relaxation would cause dilation, but the mechanism is wrong) with contraction of the ciliary muscle (correct effect on ciliary muscle).
    *   D: Contraction of the pupillary dilator muscle (correct) with contraction of the ciliary muscle (correct).
6.  **Conclusion:** The most likely effects are contraction of the pupillary dilator muscle (causing mydriasis) and contraction of the ciliary muscle. This matches option D.

