        *   Doxycycline (4 mg/kg/day divided into 2 doses, max 100 mg/day) - *Note: Doxycycline is generally avoided in children < 8 years old due to potential tooth staining, but it is recommended for Lyme disease regardless of age if it's the preferred agent or if other options are contraindicated/ineffective.*
        *   Cefuroxime axetil (30 mg/kg/day divided into 2 doses, max 600 mg/day)

