4.  **Synthesize the information:** Sudden cardiac death in a relatively young, previously healthy man points towards conditions like HCM or potentially a severe arrhythmia triggered by an underlying structural issue. Among the options, fixed obstruction of the left ventricular outflow tract (characteristic of HCM) is a well-known cause of sudden death in this demographic. The autopsy finding (though unseen) would likely confirm this.

