    *   **C: Double-stranded DNA (dsDNA):** Anti-dsDNA antibodies are characteristic of Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE). While SLE can have skin manifestations (malar rash, discoid lupus, photosensitivity, etc.), tense bullae are not a typical primary feature. The patient denies joint pain or fever, which are common in SLE.
