2.  **Identify structures in the left lateral pons:**
    *   The pons contains descending motor tracts (corticospinal tract), ascending sensory tracts, cranial nerve nuclei (V, VI, VII, VIII), pontine nuclei, and cerebellar pathways (middle cerebellar peduncle connects pons to cerebellum).
    *   The *lateral pons* specifically contains:
        *   Corticospinal tract (descending motor)
        *   Medial lemniscus (ascending sensory)
        *   Spinal trigeminal nucleus and tract (CN V sensory)
        *   Facial nucleus (CN VII motor)
        *   Abducens nucleus (CN VI motor)
