    *   **Gallstone ileus** is the most common cause of pneumobilia in the setting of bowel obstruction symptoms.
    *   In gallstone ileus, the obstruction most commonly occurs in the **distal ileum** (specifically, the ileocecal valve) because this is the narrowest part of the small intestine.
    *   Less commonly, the stone can obstruct the duodenum or jejunum, but the distal ileum is the classic location.

