    *   **ANCA-associated vasculitis (e.g., Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis, Microscopic Polyangiitis):** Can cause systemic symptoms, including skin lesions, arthritis, and sometimes eye involvement. Oral ulcers are less typical as a primary feature compared to Behçet's. ANCA (Anti-neutrophil cytoplasmic antibodies) would be positive.

