4.  **Conclusion:** The clinical picture (recurrent oral ulcers, dyspareunia suggesting genital ulcers, and uveitis) is most characteristic of Behçet's disease. Behçet's disease has a known strong association with the HLA-B51 allele. Therefore, HLA-B51 is the most likely positive finding among the choices.<unused95>B
