    *   **B: Impaired taste of the posterior 1/3 of the tongue:** Taste sensation from the posterior 1/3 of the tongue is mediated by the glossopharyngeal nerve (CN IX). While CN IX is near the parotid gland, it is generally deeper and less likely to be directly injured during a standard parotidectomy compared to the facial nerve branches. Injury is possible but less common than facial nerve injury.
