    *   C: Right umbilical artery - These carry deoxygenated blood from the fetus to the placenta. They obliterate after birth to become the medial umbilical ligaments, located on the anterior abdominal wall, not within the falciform ligament.
    *   D: Ductus arteriosus - This connects the pulmonary artery to the aorta, bypassing the fetal lungs. It obliterates after birth to become the ligamentum arteriosum, located near the base of the heart, not in the liver or falciform ligament.

