3.  **Evaluate the most likely diagnosis:** The constellation of symptoms (bradycardia, hypotension, altered mental status, bronchospasm, hypoglycemia) fits best with a beta-blocker overdose, particularly a non-selective one. The ECG findings (prolonged PR, narrow QRS) are also consistent.

