**Final Check:** The patient has microcytic anemia (low Hb, low MCV) and symptoms consistent with anemia (lethargy, pallor). This points towards chronic blood loss, likely from a parasitic infection. Hookworm (Necator americanus) is a well-known cause of significant iron deficiency anemia due to intestinal blood loss. The other options are less likely to cause this degree of anemia (Enterobius) or are less common causes (Trichuris, Taenia). Therefore, Necator americanus is the most probable answer.<unused95>A
