3.  **Consider the likely treatment:** Given the diagnosis of anemia of CKD, the standard and appropriate treatment is erythropoiesis-stimulating agents (ESAs), such as recombinant human erythropoietin (epoetin alfa) or darbepoetin alfa. These agents replace the deficient endogenous EPO.

