5.  **Conclusion:** The pathogenesis of sarcoid granulomas involves the activation of CD4+ T helper cells (Th1 phenotype) by an unknown antigen. These activated T cells release cytokines, particularly IFN-γ and TNF-α, which drive macrophage activation and granuloma formation. Therefore, TNF-α secretion by CD4+ T cells is a key component of the pathogenesis.

