    *   Improvement in the prone position and worsening in the supine position strongly suggests laryngomalacia, where floppy supraglottic structures (epiglottis, arytenoids) collapse inward during inspiration, especially when supine.
    *   Worsening with agitation or feeding is also typical of laryngomalacia due to increased respiratory effort and airflow.
