C: **Defective leukocyte adhesion (Leukocyte Adhesion Deficiency - LAD):** LAD is characterized by impaired neutrophil migration to sites of infection. Patients typically present with recurrent bacterial infections, particularly skin and mucosal infections, omphalitis (delayed cord separation), and impaired wound healing. Leukocytosis (high white blood cell count), especially neutrophilia, is characteristic, as neutrophils cannot leave the bloodstream effectively. This patient has a normal leukocyte count (7,500/mm^3) and neutrophil count (5,500/mm^3), making LAD unlikely.

