    *   The physical exam findings (soft bands in upper scrotum, pain with Valsalva) are highly suggestive of a varicocele (dilated pampiniform venous plexus). The lack of transillumination helps differentiate it from a hydrocele.
    *   Varicoceles are known to be associated with male infertility, potentially due to increased scrotal temperature impairing spermatogenesis, leading to decreased motility and abnormal morphology, as seen in this patient's semen analysis.
