    *   **D: Fusobacterium species:** These are anaerobic gram-negative rods. They do not require factors V and X for growth and are typically cultured under anaerobic conditions. They are part of the normal oral flora and can cause infections, but are less common causes of typical community-acquired pneumonia in this setting.

