5.  **Identify the abnormal region in DiGeorge syndrome:** Since DiGeorge syndrome primarily affects T-cell development due to thymic hypoplasia/aplasia, the T-cell areas of the lymph nodes will be underdeveloped or absent. The main T-cell area in the lymph node is the paracortex.

