    *   Elbow flexion: Biceps brachii (musculocutaneous nerve - C5, C6, C7) and Brachialis (musculocutaneous nerve - C5, C6, C7)
    *   Elbow extension: Triceps brachii (radial nerve - C6, C7, C8)
    *   Forearm supination/pronation: Biceps brachii (C5, C6, C7), Supinator (C6, C7), Pronator teres (C6, C7), Pronator quadratus (C8, T1)
4.  **Identify common nerve roots:** The most common nerve roots involved in these movements are C5, C6, and C7.
