    *   Whipple's disease is a rare systemic infectious disease caused by *Tropheryma whipplei*.
    *   Classic symptoms include malabsorption (diarrhea, weight loss, steatorrhea), arthralgias/arthritis, abdominal pain, and sometimes neurological or cardiac involvement.
